  "what_this_does_not_establish": [
    "One checkpoint, one noise seed. A guidance effect measured on a single seed of a single checkpoint is a direction, not a result.",
    "Decode rate is the primary read-out; a molecule can decode and still be chemically poor, which is why the property columns matter and why they are scored on the SAME SMILES rather than re-decoded.",
    "Nothing here says whether a guidance term belongs in a TRAINING loss. It acts at sampling time, so it does not change the model."
  ],
  "DO_NOT_COMPARE_ACROSS_CHECKPOINTS": "The property columns in this file are NOT comparable to cfm_checkpoint_property_benchmark.json. That panel was measured on 66 molecules from cfm_fullcorpus_2026_10_10 epoch 10; this sweep decodes 64 clouds from cfm_patience10_seed0 at midpoint/50. For reference the control arm here scores QED {'mean': 0.2358, 'std': 0.1511, 'n': 22} where the panel recorded 0.0944, and logS {'mean': -5.6993, 'std': 2.4523, 'n': 22} where the panel recorded -8.0099. Those are two different checkpoints and two different cohorts, not a property improvement. Read arms against the control of THIS sweep and nothing else."
}
